 "parsed": {
  "count": 3,
  "rationale": "Blocking memoryDump:credentialAccess, sshKey:credentialAccess and tokenCache:credentialAccess makes the target unreachable. (1) With all three parents of appServer:lateralMovement blocked, appServer is cut off, so codeRepo:collection and localAdmin:privilegeEscalation are too. (2) rdpLogin:authenticate needs tokenCache and sshKey, and ssoLogin:authenticate needs sshKey, so both die. That kills domainAdmin:privilegeEscalation, hypervisor:privilegeEscalation and monitoringHost:lateralMovement (whose parents are memoryDump, ssoLogin and rdpLogin). (3) dbLogin:authenticate needs memoryDump, so it dies, and with it fileServer:lateralMovement and secretsManager:privilegeEscalation. (4) As a result dbReplica:collection, vaultRead:collection, shareMount:collection and codeRepo:collection are all unreachable. Two blocks cannot work. Stopping the codeRepo route needs appServer, codeRepo, or all three of appServer's parents blocked. After spending one block on appServer or codeRepo, shareMount is still reachable through monitoringHost and through secretsManager. A single further block cannot stop both, plus the dbReplica routes, at once. So the minimum is 3."
 },
